Embracing DevSecOps - Integrating Security into the Software Lifecycle
Learning Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

• Understand the fundamental concepts of DevSecOps and its importance in modern software development • Implement threat modeling using LINDDUN and OWASP Threat Dragon tools • Set up and configure GitLab for secure CI/CD pipeline integration • Perform security compliance scanning using OpenSCAP • Conduct automated privacy checks using InSpec • Create a comprehensive security-integrated development workflow • Analyze and interpret security scan results to improve application security posture

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

• Basic understanding of software development lifecycle (SDLC) • Familiarity with Linux command line operations • Basic knowledge of Git version control system • Understanding of web application architecture concepts • No prior DevSecOps experience required - this lab is designed for beginners

